<title>BRAZIL: RESEARCH ALERT-Brazil Unibanco begun.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Brazil Unibanco begun.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais Securities said it had initiated coverage of Brazilian private bank Unibanco with a buy rating.</p>
<p>- also said it estimates the bank's earnings per 1,000 shares to reach $3.60 in 1997 and $4.70 in 1998.</p>
<p>- Analyst Luis Miguel Santacreu said Unibanco is undervalued given its positive earnings outlook. &quot;The bank should benefit significantly from a restructuring program begun in 1996,&quot; he said in a report.</p>
<p>- also said Unibanco is Brazil's second largest private bank in terms of loans and the fifth largest in Latin America in terms of assets.</p>
<p>- Unibanco preferred was up 1.87 percent at 43.80 reais at 1505 local/1805 GMT on the Sao Paulo bolsa.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
